From: Ashwin Devi Srinivasan <ashwin@ashds.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:12:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use the ultra-wide camera below 1x on non-SAT devices

MIUI Camera switches to the ultra-wide below 1x through the SAT or
bokeh logical cameras. When the HAL exposes neither, every mode that
offers a sub-1x zoom stays on the main camera and requests a crop
larger than its sensor, which the ISP rejects. Open the standalone
ultra-wide camera whenever the mode's saved zoom is below 1x. The
app's existing zoom conversion then scales the ratio to the
ultra-wide's field of view.

diff --git a/smali/com/android/camera/module/loader/camera2/Camera2DataContainer.smali b/smali/com/android/camera/module/loader/camera2/Camera2DataContainer.smali
index b0d5098e..daca758f 100644
--- a/smali/com/android/camera/module/loader/camera2/Camera2DataContainer.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/camera/module/loader/camera2/Camera2DataContainer.smali
@@ -665,6 +665,30 @@
 
     if-eq p2, v5, :cond_4
 
+    :try_start_uw
+    invoke-static {p2}, Lcom/android/camera/CameraSettings;->getRetainZoom(I)F
+
+    move-result v4
+
+    const/high16 v5, 0x3f800000    # 1.0f
+
+    cmpg-float v4, v4, v5
+
+    if-gez v4, :cond_uw_1
+
+    invoke-virtual {p0}, Lcom/android/camera/module/loader/camera2/Camera2DataContainer;->getUltraWideCameraId()I
+
+    move-result v4
+    :try_end_uw
+    .catchall {:try_start_uw .. :try_end_uw} :catchall_0
+
+    if-eq v4, v3, :cond_uw_1
+
+    monitor-exit p0
+
+    return v4
+
+    :cond_uw_1
     .line 9
     monitor-exit p0
 
